35. Rb2 {Now, time for one last Shankland Method of this game. How should Black proceed?} d3 {Other moves win, but this one is the cleanest by far. Black clearly wants to push the d -pawn up the board, but it looks like the pawn will now be lost following b4 , removing a defended. But... What if I do it anyway?} 36. b4 axb4 37. axb4 Nb3 38. Nxd3 (38. Qa4 Nd4 {The rest was easy for Gelfand.}) 38... Qe3+ {Black wins material.} 39. Nf2 Qc1+ {Picking up the rook. We can stop here.} *

