{Be4 Bxe4 Rxe4 Nc5 Re7 Na6} 17... Nb6 {Now, I had another opportunity to use the Shankland Method. This time, I failed to.} 18. Na5 {This would have been a better try to fight for an edge. The knight is fantastic on a5 , harassing the weak queenside pawns. Concretely, however, it looks like a bad idea because of ... Nd5 , but... Shankland method! I could have followed my own advice at the time.} (18. Nxb6 {was my move in the game.}) 18... Nd5 19. Nxb7 (19. Bxd5 $2 Bxa5 {White will lose the c3 -pawn.}) 19... Nxe3+ 20. Bxe3 {White has fantastic compensation for the missing exchange.} *

