{Black played Nd8 . What started as a harmless Berlin endgame has now become a comfortable edge for White. Though White's well-placed pieces look nice and pretty, White must turn that positional edge into something tangible. How should he continue?} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O Nxe4 5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 Nf5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. Nc3 h6 10. b3 (10. Rd1+ {This would be the punishment, immediately forcing Black into a ... Ke8 plan. Whenever Black plays with the king on e8 , he would prefer to have his pawn on h5 instead of h6 . I cover this endgame in much more detail in my Berlin LTR here on Chessable.} Ke8 11. h3 {is the most principled way for White.}) 10... Bd7 11. Bb2 Ne7 12. Rad1 Kc8 13. Rfe1 c5 14. Ne2 Nc6 15. Nf4 *

