{How should White proceed after Ne7?} 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. a3 Bxc3+ 5. bxc3 Nf6 6. e3 c5 7. cxd5 exd5 8. Bd3 O-O 9. Ne2 b6 10. O-O Ba6 11. f3 (11. dxc5 bxc5 12. Bxa6 Nxa6 13. c4 {is possible, but I was going for the transposition into an f3 -Nimzo.}) 11... Bxd3 12. Qxd3 Re8 13. Ng3 Nc6 14. Bb2 c4 15. Qe2 h5 16. Qf2 {Modern engines immediately shoot out this move as best, but this was not the case at the time of the game. I was very happy with finding this novelty, which puts the entire variation under pressure. It's even included in the Wikipedia article about the 2016 Olympiad!} Qd7 (16... h4 17. Nf5 Ne7 18. Nxh4 {is a safe capture due to} g5 19. Qg3) 17. Rae1 *

