{Now, Qxc6? was my first move out of preparation. Time to use the Shankland Method!} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Qc7 6. Be3 a6 7. Qd2 Nf6 8. O-O-O Be7 9. f3 b5 10. Kb1 h5 {So far, this is all normal theory. This particular line of the Taimanov was quite common at the time. Nowadays, the Taimanov is not super common, and when it is played, White usually does not go for the standard English Attack with Be3 , Qd2 , and O-O-O .} 11. Nxc6 *

