38... Kxd7 {Despite my far-from-perfect play, I did manage to reach this position and to find the only winning move. Time to use the Shankland Method again!} 39. Bd4 {This is clearly the move White wants to play, but it looks like it blunders allowing ... e5 . But what happens if I do it anyway?} e5 (39... Be7 {was the game continuation. One more Shankland Method moment to come!}) 40. Bxe5 {The point. Without this move, Black would be fine as is; he loses immediately.} Bxe5 41. Rxd5+ {And Black loses material.} *

