16. Be3 {Black did not play very well in the opening and early middlegame, and he is worse here, but his next move did not do him any favors.} Qe7 {Black should have saved his c5 -pawn.} (16... f5 $2 {While it is always good to ask, 'What happens if I do it anyway?', you have to not pull the trigger if the answer is 'It does not work.'} 17. Nxc5 Bxc5 18. Bxc5 Rf6 {Now, Black's plan looks pretty straightforward. Lift the rook to g6 , put the queen on d5 , tear open the long diagonal, and give mate. White should be thinking of ways to stop this from happening.}) 17. Rfe1 f5 18. Nxd6 Qxd6 {White is surely better, but it's a game. Black gets practical chances.} *

