22... Rac8 {Armenia won the 2012 Olympiad, with Russia taking second place. The two teams faced off in round 6, splitting the match 2-2, but Russia drew first blood when Kramnik beat Aronian. Here, it looks like the game might soon fizzle to a draw as everything is exchanged on the c -file, but the Shankland Method can quickly dispel that notion.} 23. Nxb7 {White would love to grab the loose pawn, but it seems properly defended. But we should always ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} Rxb7 24. Qxa6 Rbc7 25. b4 {White gets two pawns for the piece, and Black is in all kinds of pins with b5 coming next.} Qd7 26. Qb6 {White makes sure the knight remains stuck.} *

