11... Nbd7 {I was almost never playing 1.e4 at the time of this game, and I was very lucky that my opponent went right into a line that I had recently studied. I knew the right idea here, but can you find it?} 12. g4 {This is clearly the move White wants to make. Anyone who has ever played the English Attack knows that g4 - g5 is the main plan. It looks like it hangs a pawn, but we ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} Nxg4 (12... h6 13. Qg2 {White has everything under control and is ready to push.}) 13. Rg1 Nxe3 14. Qxe3 {Black has won a pawn, true. But, g7 is hanging, the king is in the center, the c4 -bishop will soon be exchanged, and White will win the battle for the d5 -square.} *

