12. b4 {What is Black's best move?} c5 {This looks ludicrous, but Black should ask: What happens if I do it anyway?} (12... a5 {In my Chessable course, I preferred this move, but with the same idea. I just wanted to lure the rook to b1 first.} 13. Rb1 c5 $1 14. bxc5 Bxf3 15. cxd6 Nd5 16. gxf3 Qg5+ 17. Kh1 Qh5 18. Be2 Nxc3 {That's why we wanted the rook on b1 .} 19. Rb3 Nxe2 20. Qxe2 Rc2 {.}) 13. bxc5 Bxf3 14. gxf3 {The reason why I prefer 12...a5 and recommend it in my course is that White can play here} (14. cxd6 Nd5 15. gxf3 Qg5+ 16. Kh1 Qh5 {and I want the rook on b1 .} 17. Be2 Nxc3 18. Rg1 {Here, there's no hanging rook on b1 .}) 14... Nxc5 15. dxc5 Rxc5 {And it transpires that White cannot break the pin in time because of the threat to take on h2 .} 16. f4 (16. Qd2 Bxh2+ $1 17. Kg2 Rg5+ 18. Kh1 Qc8 {White will be mated.}) 16... Nd5 17. Bb2 Nxc3 18. Bxc3 Qc7 19. Rfc1 Rc8 {Black gets his piece back, comfortably equalizing.} *

