{If Rb8 , not exf8=Q+ Rxf8 but c7 Rc8 exf8=Q+ Rxf8 Rxf8 . Ng6 e8=Q Kxf6 Qd8+ was Leko's try in the game.} 32... Rdc8 {Now, anything wins, but I like Morozevich's choice, because he used the Shankland Method!} 33. cxb5 {It looks like this loses a piece to ... Rxc6 . But it's clearly the move White would most like to play, so the question needs to be asked.} Rxc6 34. bxc6 Rxb1 35. fxe6 {The e -pawn is immediately decisive.} Bd3 (35... Rb8 36. c7 {hitting the rook, and e7 is coming next.}) 36. e7 Bxe4+ 37. Kg3 *

