1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 a6 6. Be3 Ng4 7. Bc1 Nf6 {After repeating moves once, I decided not to make a draw so soon.} 8. f3 Qb6 {This move does not enjoy the best reputation now, but at the time, it was considered a decent try to avoid the mainline English Attack. In the same Olympiad just a few days prior, Dominguez demolished Mamedyarov in this line in the Cuba-Azerbaijan match. Perhaps it was part of team Azerbaijan's preparation, as Safarli then chose it against me in the critical final round.} 9. Be2 {This move was extremely rare at the time, but I had an idea in mind.} *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
