1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Be7 5. Bf4 O-O 6. e3 c5 7. dxc5 Bxc5 8. a3 Nc6 9. Qc2 Qa5 10. Rd1 Be7 11. Be2 dxc4 12. Bxc4 Nh5 13. O-O Nxf4 14. exf4 g6 15. g3 Rd8 16. Rxd8+ Qxd8 17. Rd1 Bd7 {At this point, Kramnik clearly should be trying to use his lead in development. Eventually, the bishop pair and White's slightly compromised pawn structure could matter, but for the moment, Black is playing without his a8 -rook, and the queen is in the line of fire.} *

