{Moving on a bit deeper into my career, I got to demonstrate the Shankland Method in action in one of my favorite games I've ever played.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. O-O Nc6 8. d5 Ne7 9. Ne1 Nd7 10. Nd3 f5 11. f3 f4 12. Bd2 g5 13. Rc1 Ng6 {The battle lines have been drawn. White clearly wants to break through on the queenside, while Black tries to give mate on the kingside. The break I want to make is c5 .} *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Level 3"]
[Black "Shankland-Nyzhnyk Exercise #1"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "r1bq1rk1/pppnn1bp/3p4/3Pp1p1/2P1Pp2/2NN1P2/PP1BB1PP/2RQ1RK1 b - - 0 13"]
[PlyCount "6"]

13... Ng6 {The battle lines have been drawn. White clearly wants to break through on the queenside, while Black tries to give mate on the kingside. The break I want to make is c5 .} 14. c5 {Shankland Method! What happens if I do it anyway? In the game, Black took me at my word and did not take the pawn.} (14. b4 $6 {This move guarantees c5 will come next, but it is slow and will not help White win the game on the queenside once c5 comes. As such, it is wasted time.} Nf6 15. c5 h5 {and ... g4 is coming quickly. I would be worried with White here.}) 14... dxc5 {Obviously, we should know what to do if Black takes the pawn before we push c4 - c5 . With energetic play, White retains a clear edge.} (14... Nf6 {Now, ideally, we would like to slam cxd6 and Nb5 to invade the queenside, but this allows a check on b6 . How can we use the Shankland Method?}) (14... Nxc5 {This was possible, but after} 15. Nxc5 dxc5 {, instead of} 16. b4 cxb4 17. Nb5 Rf7 {and Black can protect the 7th rank, Na4! b6 b4! cxb4} 18. Bxb4 {where I prefer White's position despite the pawn less. He has successfully opened the queenside, and his pieces are very active.}) 15. b4 {This is the best way to tear open the queenside. It looks like it loses a pawn, but what happens if I do it anyway?} cxb4 16. Nb5 {Despite the two pawns up, Black is in bad shape. White will easily take back the lost material, and the queenside is being blasted open.} *

