23... Bd7 {Now what?} 24. Rfc1 {We want to develop the f1 rook, but obviously, we have to deal with the threat of ... Bxc6 . But... What happens if I do it anyway? This turns out to be very strong, and Black cannot take on c6 .} Bxc6 (24... g4 $1 {Black has to try. He has no other plan. He is still okay here, but should be very precise.  A)} 25. fxg4 {is not the right call. The c6 -rook won't be immune to capture forever!} f3 26. gxf3 Bxc6 27. dxc6 Nxf3+ {is not working for White.  B) hxg4 hxg4 Nxg4 Qg5? Time to use the Shankland method once more in our next exercise! Qg6 This would have been better, avoiding the issue in the game.}) 25. dxc6 {With Bc4 and Nc3 - Nd5 on the way, White is totally winning despite the exchange less.} *

