26... bxc6 {Black's position looks a bit suspect, but it is still fairly solid. How should White continue?} 27. c5 {This is definitely the move White wants to play. He prevents ... c5 , which fixes the c6 -pawn on a light square and solidifies the knight on d4 . I'm sure Ivanisevic saw this move and rejected it due to the ... Nd5 response. But we should always ask: What happens if I do it anyway?} (27. Rd1 $6 c5 $1 {White is definitely still better, but he missed his chance to end the game on the spot.}) 27... Nd5 28. Qc4 {Black cannot take on e3 yet because the knight is pinned.} dxc5 29. Qxc5 Nxe3 {Now, for the moment, it might look like things have gone wrong. But when one looks a bit closer, White has a crushing initiative.} 30. Qd6 {Simple and totally crushing. Black can hardly defend the bishop in a reasonable way.} Rad8 31. Bxa4 {Black is done for.} *

