6... g5 {I always admired the aggression and fearlessness in Judit's play. Here she is, playing Black against the greatest player who ever lived; all of her pieces are on the back rank, and she just goes for it. That said... this is not a good move, and it can be punished by using the Shankland Method.} 7. d4 {When Black is so underdeveloped, White obviously wants to blow up the center. It looks like this move is ill-advised because once ... g4 comes, the knight will be kicked away, and White will lose a pawn. But we always ask, 'What happens if I do it anyway?'} g4 8. Nfd2 (8. Ne1 $2 Ba6 $1 {is a bit annoying.}) (8. Ng5 h6 {is not an option.}) 8... cxd4 9. cxd4 exd4 10. Nc4 {Black won a central pawn, but the position is opening far faster than she would like.} *

