{However, had Judit played Rb8! , her position is still quite bad according to the machine, but I think it will take a lot of work for White to finish her off when b4 does not come so easily.} 13... d5 {Now, where should the knight go?} 14. Nd6+ ({Forward, of course! It looks like this loses a pawn, but we should ask, what happens if I do it anyway? Playing} 14. Nd2 {would lead White nowhere.}) 14... Kf8 {Judit correctly chose not to take on d6 . Her position is lost either way, but avoiding the capture certainly gives her more practical chances, as we will see later on. Now, how should White continue? Garry clearly saw the right idea since he played it on the following move, but he did not need to wait.} (14... Bxd6 15. exd6 Qxd6 16. b4 {again, what if I do it anyway? Black's pawn center crumbles, and she will be crushed after} Ne7 17. bxc5 Qxc5 18. Bb2 {or c4 Qxd4} f6 {.}) 15. b4 {White should play this while he still can.} (15. Bf4 $6 {This is second best.} h5 16. b4 $1 {This time, Garry did not need to be asked twice.}) *

