30. Rae1 {Now, Black is very, very lost. The machine gives +4. But Judit absolutely found the best move in practical terms.} f5 {This move looks suicidal. Black allows exf6 , winning a pawn, opening up her king, and opening the e -file for White's rook. But we ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} 31. exf6 Qh7 {All of a sudden, things are not so clear. White is surely winning with best play, but the position is very messy and has to be calculated well. With the clocks ticking down, Kasparov himself was unable to find the way cleanly.} *

