1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 Be7 {This was sort of the main line.} (7... a6 {is my recommendation in my Classical Sicilian LTR.}) 8. O-O-O O-O 9. f4 h6 10. Bh4 e5 11. Nf5 {At this point, I realized I was about to play a wildly complicated game.} (11. Nxc6 bxc6 12. fxe5 dxe5 13. Qxd8 Rxd8 14. Rxd8+ Bxd8 15. Bc4 {This looked a bit vegetarian to me during the game. The engine likes White by some small margin, but even with this knowledge, I believe Black is pretty much okay}) 11... Bxf5 12. exf5 Qa5 {Now, I was a bit too aggressive with my use of the Shankland Method here. What should White play?} *

