12... Qa5 {Now, I was a bit too aggressive with my use of the Shankland Method here. What should White play?} 13. Bc4 {Developing a new piece and increasing the pressure on the d5 -square was simple, strong, and clearly best. This is now a very good bishop, and Black is quite a bit worse. Black misses the bishop on e6 you find in the Najdorf.} (13. g4 {This was too aggressive and unnecessary. Black could have used the Shankland Method against me!} Ne4 $1 14. Nxe4 Qxa2 {and White should bail out into a balanced endgame.}) *

