19... Qc7 {This was a serious try. While objectively a stronger move than the game continuation (which was the fighter's way of resisting), it leads to a really miserable and quite simple position. How should White proceed?} 20. Rd2 {This is necessary, so ... Nb4 does not come with tempo. It looks like a bad idea because it walks straight into ... Bf4 , but we should always ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} (20. Kb1 $6 Nb4 $1 {This is much less convincing. Black wins a tempo by threatening c2 , and he is ready to play ... f6 next. White is better, but the game goes on.}) 20... Bf4 (20... Nb4 $2 21. f6) 21. Nf6+ Kh8 22. Qh5+ Bh6 23. Ng4 {Black now has major problems with the king, and White is ready to take on h6 . Black can avoid mate but at a heavy cost.} Qf4 24. Nxh6 Qxh6 {Now, it should be pretty clear that the black king will survive. So, we cash in.} 25. Qxh6+ gxh6 26. Bg2 {Black was able to exchange the queens, but he'll lose the d4 -pawn. White should have excellent winning chances in this rook ending.} *

