1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. g3 d5 4. Bg2 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. b3 a5 7. Nc3 c6 8. d4 (8. Bb2 {is more precise.}) 8... Nbd7 9. Qc2 b6 10. e4 Ba6 11. Nd2 ({Stronger is} 11. e5 Ne8 12. Ne2 {and White is in control.}) 11... c5 12. exd5 cxd4 13. Nb5 exd5 14. Nxd4 Rc8 15. Re1 b5 16. Bb2 Re8 17. Qd1 {White has not played a particularly inspired Catalan thus far, and Qd1 - c2 - d1 is not a good sign. Still, it takes a lot of work for Black to take over the initiative.} bxc4 18. bxc4 Qb6 19. Rb1 {Now, Black has a very powerful idea. It's clear what we want to do, but we need to use the Shankland Method to make it work.} *

