1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 a6 5. e3 Bf5 6. Nh4 (6. Qb3 {is my recommendation in my Chessable 1.d4 LTR, and I stand by it.}) 6... Bg4 7. Qc2 e6 8. h3 Bh5 9. g4 Nfd7 10. Ng2 Bg6 11. Qb3 b5 12. c5 a5 13. Nf4 b4 14. Nxg6 hxg6 15. Na4 Na6 16. a3 Be7 17. Bd2 O-O 18. Bd3 e5 19. O-O Nc7 20. axb4 Rb8 21. Nb6 axb4 22. Nxd7 Qxd7 23. Ra7 Bf6 24. dxe5 Bxe5 25. Bxb4 Qd8 26. f4 Qh4 {I had played a less than stellar game to this point, but sort of lucked into a good position. Now, White clearly has to play either Rf3 or Kg2 to keep things under control on the kingside. I chose the wrong one.} *

