27. Rf3 {Now, how should Black play?} Ne6 {This is the move Black wants to make to bring more pieces into the attack. It ignores the threat to the bishop, but what happens if I do it anyway?} 28. fxe5 (28. Qa3 Qf6 $1 {Another strong move. Black retreats the queen to stop the threat of fxe5 , and now b2 is hanging as well. We'll continue in our next exercise.}) 28... Ng5 {White will be mated.} *

