29. Rf2 {This was too ambitious. Now, how should Black respond?} Nxf4 {I fell victim to my own method. Black clearly wants to take on f4 , but it looks like the response Bf1 would be a problem. He should ask: What if I do it anyway?} 30. Bf1 (30. exf4 $2 {This one is easier to disarm.} Bd4 {White collapses immediately.}) 30... Qh4 31. exf4 (31. Rxf4 Qg3+ 32. Bg2 {Now what? We'll see this in our next exercise.}) 31... Bd4 32. Be1 (32. Qf3 Rxb4) 32... Rfe8 {Black wins.} *

