32. Bg2 {Now what?} d4 {This was a winner. White's rook is bullied off the f4 -square, and then the queen will reach h2 .} (32... Rxb4 $2 33. Rxb4 Qe1+ 34. Bf1 Qg3+ 35. Bg2 Qe1+ 36. Bf1 g5 $1 {I was very surprised to see Black decline a draw here, but then I realized in horror what he had in mind. ... Bg3 is coming next, and I no longer have Rf4 ! The immediate Bg3 was met by} 37. Rf4 {.}) 33. Rf3 Qh2+ 34. Kf1 dxe3 {Black is ready to follow up with ... e2 .} 35. Rxe3 ({Or} 35. Qxe3 Rxb4 {.}) 35... Qf4+ {Black wins the bishop on b4 , allowing him to continue his attack with equal material. White is done for.} *

