{White takes on f7 and saves the game. E.g., Be5 Qxf7 Bg7 . This sequence is not easy to find!} {I was very surprised to see Black decline a draw here, but then I realized in horror what he had in mind. mind. ... Bg3 is coming next, and I no longer have Rf4 anymore!} 36... g5 37. Ra8 {This was the only convincing way to hold.} (37. e4 $2 dxe4 $1 38. Rc4 Qd2 $1 {Well spotted. Black wins a tempo by threatening mate on h2 , and he stops my rook from reaching the c2 -square. White's point was Bg3?} 39. Qf3 Qb4 40. Qg3) (37. Qb3 {simply allowed} Bg3 38. Qc2 Qxb4 {.}) 37... Rxa8 38. Qxa8+ Kh7 39. Qa3 Bg3 40. Qd3+ g6 41. Qe2 Qxb4 42. Qf3 *

