43. Re4 {Now, Black is winning, but he should be precise. Using the Shankland Method could have done him a favor here.} Qd1+ {This is the move Black wants to play, but it looks like I have things under control after Kf2 . But always ask, what if I do it anyway?} (43... Bxb2 $2 {This was a big mistake. The idea was to force my queen to the undefended b1 -square to be able to give a check on d1 next, but I have an unexpected resource.} 44. Rd7 $1 {Black clearly missed this resource, and now it's a game again. Other moves just lose: Qa2} e1=Q+ {or Qb1? Qd1+ Kf2 Qxb1 .}) ({After} 43... Bg3 44. Rxe2 Qxe2 {, Black is better, but it would take a Magnus Carlsen to win this.}) 44. Kf2 Bd4+ 45. Kg3 Bxc5 {A silent but deadly killer. The twin threats of ... Bxa7 and ... Qd6 prove impossible to meet, and White is crushed.} ({b4 Bxa7 Raa4 Qd6+ Kf3} 45... Qd3+) *

