{Shankland Method! If gxh3 , the queen reaches h4 , and White wins after Qh4 . Qe4 wins as well, but it is not nearly as clean.} 52... Rd8+ {What should White play?} 53. Bd3 {This is clearly the move I want to make, blocking the check and stopping it forever. It looks like this simply lets the h -pawn through, but the Shankland Method makes it work.} Qa1 {Now, after having suffered in a miserable position for hours on end, I saw my chance to make a draw and took it right away. This was foolish. I could have used the Shankland Method again and even won the game!} (53... h2 54. Qe4 $1 {And all of a sudden, Black cannot stop the twin mate threats of Qh7 and Qe8 . The machine claims it is forced mate.} h1=Q 55. Qe8+ Rxe8 56. Rxe8# {I would have so loved to reach this final position.}) 54. Re3 {The rook going to h3 with mate is not a small threat!} ({The game continued} 54. Qe4 $2 Qa5+ {and a draw by perpetual check was agreed soon.}) 54... g4 {Now, what does White really want to play?} 55. Rxh3+ *

