1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 6. Re1 b5 7. Bb3 O-O 8. h3 Bb7 9. d3 d5 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Nbd2 Qd7 {Nowadays, this position is fairly well known, but it was not at back in 2015. Anand had taken on e5 and beaten Aronian, but Black could improve, as was shown in this game.} 12. Nxe5 Nxe5 13. Rxe5 (13. Rxe5 Nf6 {was Aronian's choice, but it does not fully equalize, and Vishy won a nice game after} 14. Nf3 Bd6 15. Re1 {.}) *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
