[PlyCount "6"]

13. Rxe5 {How should Black proceed?} Nf4 (13... Nf6 {was Aronian's choice, but it does not fully equalize and Vishy won a nice game after} 14. Nf3 Bd6 15. Re1 {.}) 14. Nf3 {Now, Black has a couple of tempting options. What is the best one?} Nxg2 {This is definitely the one Black would like to play most, taking the most critical pawn around White's king and luring him to the long diagonal. It looks like Black's pieces cannot join the attack too fast, but what happens if I do it anyway?} 15. Kxg2 a5 {This is a very effective follow-up that leaves White in horrible shape. Black gains an incidental tempo by threatening ... a4 , taking the b3 bishop, and equalizing material when the monster on b7 will reign supreme. Once White parries this threat, ... Ra6 will come to smash the kingside.} *

