[PlyCount "12"]

20. Bc2 {Now, Black has to be careful - there is only one winning move, and he needs to use the Shankland Method to find it. What would you play?} Rd8 {This is clearly the move Black wants to play, bringing his last piece out and getting ready to take on d5 . It looks like this blunders Bg5 but always ask...} 21. Bg5 (21. Qe1 {The move Ivanchuk played in the game loses every which way, but his position was beyond salvation anyway.} Qd7 22. Ng5 h6 23. Ne4 Rg6+ 24. Kh2 f5 25. Ng3 Qxd5 26. Qg1 Qf3 {White had seen enough. ... Rxg3 is coming next, and} 27. Be3 {is met by} Qxe3 {.}) 21... Rxd5 22. Bxf6 Qxf6 23. Qe2 {If you saw the right move in advance, good on you! If you didn't, find it now.} Re5 {No mate for you, and Black takes on f3 next.} 24. Qd3 Bxf3+ 25. Qxf3 Rg5+ {Over.} *

