1. Nf3 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. d4 c6 5. Bg5 h6 (5... dxc4 6. e4 b5 7. e5 h6 8. Bh4 g5 9. Bg3 Nd5 {is the standard Botvinnik order.}) 6. Bh4 dxc4 7. e4 g5 8. Bg3 b5 9. Be2 Bb7 10. e5 Nh5 11. a4 a6 {White has sacrificed a pawn and needs to look for attacking chances. How should he continue?} *

