{I played board 1 for the United States in the 2015 World Team Championship- it was always a lifelong goal of mine to lead the US Team, and something I dreamed of for as long as I could remember. In the last-round match against Cuba, I had a fascinating game with Lenier Dominguez.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Bb5+ {This is a funky sideline, but nobody has anything against the Grunfeld anyway. So, people try stuff like this!} c6 8. Ba4 O-O 9. Ne2 b5 10. Bb3 a5 11. a4 Nd7 12. e5 Nb6 13. axb5 cxb5 14. h4 {I clearly was in no mood to mess around this game. The machine is not too stoked about my attacking possibilities, but it does not seem like an easy position for Black to play. What would you do?} *

