[PlyCount "10"]

19. Qg3 {This was possible, but I calculated a variation that I did not like for White. Can you find the way for Black?} Nxc3 {This is definitely the move Black wants to play. When you start calculating, it might look like there is a problematic tactical resource for White, but always ask... What if I do it anyway?} 20. Bxe6 (20. Nxc3 Bxb3) 20... Nxe2 21. Rh8+ {This looks like a major problem, but when one peels back the layers, we realize that Black is quite fine.} (21. Qxg6 $2 Qxe6 {because White's previous move didn't come with a check.}) 21... Kxh8 (21... Bxh8 $2 22. Qxg6+ {White mates.}) 22. Qh3+ Kg8 23. Bxc8 Nxd4 {Unfortunately, despite taking Black's queen, I am not better here. He will take a fair amount of material back.} *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Level 4"]
[Black "Shankland-Dominguez Perez Exe"]
