37... Ra1 {Right before time control, I missed my one big chance. What should White do?} 38. f5 {This was a winner. White's best hope of winning the rook endgame lies in advancing the pawn to f6 to fix f7 as a long-term weakness. It looks like Black can simply take the pawn, but we have to ask: What if I do it anyway?} (38. Rc8+ Kg7 {The chance is gone, and now Black is making an easy draw.}) 38... gxf5 39. gxf5 exf5 40. d5 {The answer is that White slams his pawn through to promotion, and Black can't stop it.} ({Rd1} 40. Rd3 $1 {White will win the pawn endgame.}) ({Kf8 d6 Ke8} 40. Rc8+ {Kd7 Rc7+ Ke8 Kf4 White wins.}) *

