1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. e4 d6 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Be2 e6 8. O-O exd5 9. exd5 Bg4 10. Bf4 a6 11. Qd2 Qb6 12. Rae1 Bxf3 13. Bxf3 Nbd7 14. b3 Rfe8 15. g4 Qb4 16. Bxd6 (16. Nb1 {Was probably prudent}) 16... Nxg4 17. Ne4 Qxd2 18. Nxd2 Nge5 19. Bg2 Nd3 20. Re7 Rxe7 21. Bxe7 Bf6 22. Bxf6 Nxf6 23. Rd1 b6 {This is quite a tough position for White to play and find the best way, and I burned half an hour here. I calculated very well, but not perfectly. I got to use the Shankland Method several times to make sure I was making the right decision.} (23... Rd8 {was better, e.g.} 24. Nb1 Nf4 25. Nc3 b6 26. Na4 Nd7 {.}) *

