29... g5 {This tempting move is met with a beautiful response.} 30. Rxd4 {Getting rid of the annoying knight.} (30. Bf5 {is the move we'd love to play, but here, the bishop can be captured.}) 30... cxd4 31. Bf5 {With complete domination. White does not have an immediate threat, but Ne5 - c6 hanging over Black's head means that none of his pieces can move. White can slowly come up the board with Kf1 - e2 - d3 , take on d4 , and push b4 and c5 .} *

