21... Bxe5 {Up to here, the game has been very well played, and it never swayed from being balanced. While White is not better yet, I definitely found the best move to put my opponent under pressure.} 22. Rf7 {This is the move White wants to make, invading the seventh rank. It looks ludicrous because Black will take on d4 , grabbing a full bishop with a discovered check. But we have to ask: What happens if I do it anyway?} Bxd4+ (22... Bf4+ $2 {does not work.} 23. Kd3 Bxc1 24. Rxd7+ Kc8 25. Ra7 {Black is up an exchange, but his rooks are frozen due to skewer threats on the back rank. He may well lose all four of his pawns in the upcoming moves.}) 23. Kd3 {And now we see the point. Black has a lot of threats to deal with! Rxd7 +, Kxd4 , and Bxc6 . He is still okay, but a lot of accuracy is needed. My opponent managed to a point.} Kb6 24. Rxd7 ({And Black restores the balance with Re3} 24. Kxd4 Re4+ {followed by ... Rxa4 .}) *

