1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 a6 5. a4 e6 6. Bg5 h6 7. Bh4 dxc4 8. e3 {Black has won a pawn for the moment. But White is hoping to take back on c4 next and claim a slight edge thanks to his more active pieces. How should Black proceed?} *

