[Black "Van Wely-Topalov Exercise #2"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "3qk1r1/R4p2/4p2p/1p3p2/1bpPbP2/1n2PN2/1P3KPP/3Q1B1R w - - 0 20"]
[PlyCount "8"]

20. Ra2 {This was a mistake, and now Black has a fantastic idea.} e5 {This is the move Black wants to make to blow up the center and open lines to White's king. It looks outrageous- the pawn has no defenders, and 3 white pieces can take it. But... What if I do it anyway? It turns out White has no good captures available.} 21. fxe5 ({The d -pawn can't capture because now the white queen is unprotected.} 21. Nxe5 Qh4+ $1 22. g3 Rxg3 $1 {Black is crashing through.} 23. hxg3 Qxh1 {and ... Qh2 will be mate next. White's only defense to the immediate mate threat does not save the game.} 24. Nf3 Bxf3 $1 25. Qxf3 Be1+ $1 26. Ke2 Nc1+ $1 {Black wins the queen and the game.}) 21... f4 {Of course, the initiative continues.} 22. exf4 {This doesn't help either. Once Black's queen enters the game from the d4 -square, White will not survive.} (22. Be2 {was Loek's choice, and probably the best move.}) 22... Bxf3 23. gxf3 (23. Qxf3 Qxd4+ 24. Qe3 Qd5 $1 {White can't do anything about ... Bc5 coming next.}) 23... Bd2 {...Qxd4 is coming next, and it's all over but the crying.} *

