13. Bxh6 {White's last move was a mistake. I had seen what was coming but misevaluated the resulting position. How should Black continue?} Nxe4 {What happens if I do it anyway? Black pitches the knight to make room for his queen to reach h4 .} 14. Nxe4 Qh4+ 15. g3 Qxh6 16. Qxh6 Bxh6 17. Nxd6 Re5 {Black is absolutely fine in this endgame, and in fact, his position is even a bit more pleasant. I defended well to a point, but I allowed my opponent a big chance right before time control. I didn't show the first moves of the game as an introduction because that would sort of give you a little bit of a hint about the point of this exercise. A usual, you can check the full game after the exercises.} *

