16... Nd7 {I got a very pleasant position straight out of the opening, but at this point, I missed the cleanest way through. Can you do better?} 17. exf5 {This was a crusher. It is definitely the move White wants to play, tearing open the e -file while Black is forced to take back with a piece on f5 and leave himself with a weakness on e6 .} (17. Bh4 $6 {Not bad, but definitely not best either.}) 17... Nxf5 {But what now?} 18. g4 {This is the move White wants to make. Kick the knight, bully it back to h6 , and then Ng5 comes to win the house. It looks like it hangs the d4 -pawn. But... what if I do it anyway?} (18. Ng5 {directly is messier.}) 18... Bxf3 (18... Nh6 19. Ng5 {is crushing.}) 19. Qxf3 Nxd4 (19... Nh6 {This should be preferred, but after} 20. Bd2 {with Rae1 to follow, Black is quite busted all the same.}) 20. Qe4 {I somehow missed this move in my calculations. White wins a piece with the twin threats on d4 and h7 .} *

