13. g4 {Black has an important choice to make. Do we sacrifice on g4 or retreat to g6 ?} Nxg4 (13... Bg6 $6 {This was not terrible, but it was better to go for it.} 14. Re1 {This is not a subtle move. White wants e4 - e5 . How should Black respond? Question for our next exercise!}) 14. hxg4 Bxg4 15. Qe1 {It's easy to get this far in your calculations and stop. White breaks the pin; he is ready for Qe3 next. He is a piece up, and it is hard to imagine the attack succeeding. But... always ask, what happens if I do it anyway!} (15. Nb3 {The machine prefers this move, which looks weird to me, and Black has good compensation. I'm sure that Svidler was not worried about it, and concerned only with Qe1 , breaking the pin.}) 15... Bg5 {An important move, without which Black would be worse. Qe3 is prevented, and the attack rages on.} 16. Nxg5 {What else? White could barely move.} Nxd4 {White is in trouble.} *

