12. f4 {White just pushed f2 - f4 , gaining space on the kingside and the center and threatening to take on g5 . What should Black do?} O-O-O {Of course, this is the move Black wants to make. It looks like it loses the g5 -pawn, but we have to ask: What if I do it anyway?} 13. fxg5 {Going pawn-grabbing is a bad idea.} (13. Nd3 {Hikaru wisely avoided taking the pawn.}) (13. g4 Be4 $1 {This is the best square for the bishop. It looks like it hangs f7 . But we have to ask, what if I do it anyway?} 14. fxg5 c5 $1 {White's center comes under direct assault. And once the center falls, Black's pieces will all converge on White's vulnerable king.} 15. c3 c4 $1 16. Nd2 Nxe5 $1 17. dxe5 hxg5 {Black's pieces rush into the attack, and White is done for.}) {My plan was hxg5 Rxf7 Nxe5 dxe5 Bg7 Rxg7 Qxe5 Also good for Black, but 14... c5 ! was stronger.} 13... hxg5 14. Bxg5 f6 {The pawn is immune from capture thanks to h2 hanging. Black will take back his pawn and White's kingside is collapsing.} *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "?"]
[White "Level 5"]
