21. b4 {Now what? Ask the right question and you'll get the right answer.} Rad8 {Obviously, Black would like to bring his last piece into the game on the open file. It looks like this drops the b7 -pawn with tempo, but we know what to ask.} 22. Nxb7 Bc4 23. Nxd8 Bxf1 24. Qxf1 Rxf2 {Of course, Black does not settle for taking the knight on d8 and remaining two pawns down.} 25. Qg1 Ra2 {Black wins material.} 26. Rxa2 (26. Qxa7 Qxg2#) 26... Bxg1 ({Kxg1} 26... Qc1 {The computer sees no difference, but I believe Levon's move is stronger than Qxd8 .}) *

