{Rxc3 bxc3 Bxe4 Bg2± I don't buy this exchange sacrifice, but Black didn't have much of a choice. The first rule of any exchange sacrifice is to always ask, 'How good are the rooks?' Here, the rook will not be so terrible.} 12... Rc8 {This was not played in the game but is interesting and relevant all the same. How should White proceed?} 13. g6 {Always ask, what happens if I do it anyway? This is clearly the move White wants to make.} (13. Qd2 {is too slow and met by} Ne5 {.}) (13. Bh3 {is also met by} Ne5 {.}) (13. Rh3 {is not bad here, but g6 is more to the point.}) (13. Rg1 {is also too slow and allows} g6 {.}) 13... hxg6 ({Or} 13... fxg6 14. Nxe6 {.}) 14. hxg6 Rxh1 15. gxf7+ Kxf7 ({Black should play this one, but he's definitely worse. It's critical to see that} 15... Ke7 {fails to} 16. Qg4 {and} Nc5 {is not possible due to} 17. Bg5+ {.}) 16. Qf3+ Nf6 17. Qxh1 *

