23... Kd8 {Now, Black is ready for ... Nf5 , ... Ne8 , or ... Kc7 and ... Rae8 . White should be very energetic to win the game.} 24. Ne4 {This is the move we want to play to maximize our activity. It looks like there are tactical problems. But always ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} (24. Bh3 $2 Ne8) 24... Kc7 (24... Nf5 {is the scariest reply, and we'll deal with it in our next exercise.}) (24... Bxd5 25. Nf6 $1 Bxg2 26. Nxg8) 25. Nf6 {This looks like it hangs g7 . But.. . what happens if I do it anyway?} Rxg7 (25... Nxf6 26. gxf6 Rae8 27. Rxe8 Rxe8 28. Be5 $1 {Black can barely move, and White has endless threats. The simplest is b3 followed by c4 .}) 26. Re7 ({It's important to bring the rook in and not to capture with the knight on e7 . Black is in big trouble as Rxg5 runs into Rxd7++- . After Rd8 , the computer is a savage and plays f4 here, but} 26. Nxd7 Rxg5 27. Nc5 Kb8 28. Bf3 {is quite enough in human terms.}) ({But not} 26. Nxd7 Rxg5 {and Black is back in the game.}) *

