1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 3. Nf3 Nf6 4. Nc3 e6 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Bd3 dxc4 7. Bxc4 b5 8. Bd3 Bd6 9. O-O O-O 10. Qc2 Bb7 11. a3 Rc8 12. Ng5 {It is every Meran player's dream to play a game like this one. White has just played Ng5 , threatening the pawn on h7 . What should we do?} ({We have already seen} 12. b4 {where} a5 {is the move I recommended in my Semi-Slav LTR, and Kasimdzhanov dropped a novelty against Topalov.}) *

