12. Ng5 {It is every Meran player's dream to play a game like this one. White has just played Ng5 , threatening the pawn on h7 . What should we do?} c5 {The Shankland Method strikes again. Black seemingly could not advance ... c5 because it hangs b5 and ignores the threat to h7 , but always ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} 13. Nxh7 {White grabs a pawn with tempo.} (13. Bxh7+ {Modern theory suggests this is a better move, but Black still has good play, for example, after} Kh8 14. f4 cxd4 15. exd4 g6 {The game is very complicated. I covered this position and the entire opening line in more detail in my Semi-Slav course.}) 13... Ng4 {Shankland Method again! Black pays no need to the hanging rook on f8 and sends everything at White's kingside.} 14. f4 (14. Nxf8 Bxh2+ 15. Kh1 Qh4 {and mate.}) 14... cxd4 15. exd4 {The next move is one of the toughest ones, but once you put yourself in your dream world where anything is possible, you can ask, what happens if I do it anyway?} Bc5 {Black goes after the d4 -pawn.} *

