1. c4 b6 2. e4 Bb7 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. f3 c5 5. Nge2 e6 6. d4 cxd4 7. Nxd4 Nc6 8. Be3 {I had only remembered checking ... Bc5 here and knew the best plan was to castle long. The way he played, I could have just been slightly better in a normal hedgehog, but I was feeling feisty and wanted to play my second Sicilian with White despite never opening with 1. e4 .} Be7 (8... Bc5 9. Nxc6 Bxc6 10. Bxc5 bxc5 11. Qd2 {White has very easy play with O-O-O , Qe3 , Rd2 . Everything is perfectly secure on the queenside; ... d5 will never come, and then Be2 , Rhd1 , g4 , etc.- seems very nice for me.} O-O 12. O-O-O Rb8 13. Qe3 {and so on.}) 9. Qd2 (9. Be2 {On another day, I might have gone for this.} O-O 10. O-O {White has a nice hedgehog, but Black is solid. I was in a violent mood and knew Nikita was much better in more strategic positions.}) 9... O-O 10. O-O-O Ne5 {Now I started to misplay the position.} 11. f4 {Not the best way.} (11. Ndb5 $5 {also was not bad, though it looks very risky after} Rc8 12. b3 d5 13. Nxa7 dxc4) (11. Bf4 $1 {This was best. I disliked} Ng6 12. Bg3 Nh5 {but somehow missed that after the simple} 13. Bf2 {, Black does not get ... Bg5 .}) 11... Neg4 (11... Ng6 {I thought this was coming, in the style of the Taimanov. After} 12. e5 Ng4 13. h4 $1 {The position is very unclear, but Black should not be worse. Note that Bg1? runs into} Nxf4) 12. e5 Ne4 13. Nxe4 Bxe4 {I had seen this position when I played f4 and thought I would be better after Bg1 , threatening Qe2 , but only now realized ... d5 would come.} 14. Be2 {Right after I made my last move, I realized it was a mistake thanks to the Shankland Method. Luckily, it went unpunished.} (14. h3 $1 {This should have been preferred. I wanted to get this position with my bishop on e2 instead of f3 , but for obvious reasons, this was the better way. After} Nxe3 15. Qxe3 Bb7 16. Kb1 {, the computer likes Black, but I have a hard time believing White can be worse.}) (14. Bg1 $2 d5 $1 {and Black is just better.}) *

