14. Be2 {Right after I made my last move, I realized it was a mistake thanks to the Shankland Method. Luckily, it went unpunished.} Bb4 {I might have resigned on move 14 with White. This move, which I did not even notice until the computer pointed it out after the game, wins on the spot! A rare case of mutual blindness from 2700+ players.} (14... f5 $2 15. exf6 Nxf6 16. Bd3 {I thought I was better here, but the computers laugh.}) (14... Rc8 $5 {This is also horrendous for White. While this move does not end the game, it is very, very strong. Black clearly wants to bring the rook into the game, but this means ignoring White's threat to the knight on g4 . But we ask: What if I do it anyway? The answer is actually that it works, and works very easily.}) 15. Qxb4 Nxe3 {White is in terrible shape.} *

