29. Rd1 {Black is now in a very tough spot, but he can keep the fight going if he plays correctly. What would you do?} exf5 {The best practical try. This move looks insane. Who in their right mind would allow the queen to reach e8 ? I did not take it very seriously. But we always ask... What if I do it anyway? It turns out White does not have a clean win.} (29... Qe7 $2 30. Qxb5 Rb6 31. Qd7) 30. Qe8+ Bf8 31. Rd7 (31. Rd8 Rf6) 31... Qc8 32. Qf7+ Kh8 33. Bb2 Rg6 ({At first, I thought I was winning on the spot with} 33... Rc7 {Qd8} 34. Qxf5 {, but I missed Rg5 . Black's position looks very scary, but White does not have a win. I was quite annoyed to realize that I would have to win the game all over again!}) *

