26. b3 {What would you play here?} c3 {This is obviously the move Black wants to play. It looks like it is begging to get checkmated by Qe2 - Qa6 . But we know what to ask!} 27. Qe2 Qd4 {Again, what happens if I do it anyway? Black clearly wants to centralize the queen, and we now see that, in fact, the king is not in any danger at all. He will safely hide on b6 .} 28. Qb5 (28. Qa6+ Kc7 29. Qb7+ Kd6 {Black's king is safe as can be, and he will win the game with the c3 -pawn.}) 28... Kc7 (28... Rd6 {was fine, too, but I like this one more. It plays in the same spirit as Black would have to if White had checked on a6 the previous move instead. The king is totally safe, and White is lost.}) *

