1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 a6 8. O-O-O Bd7 9. f3 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 Be7 11. h4 b5 12. Kb1 Qc7 13. Qd2 {The ... h5 idea works against other moves.} (13. g4 h5) (13. Be3 h5) 13... h6 14. Be3 h5 {This strikes me as incorrect. Black loses a tempo, as I explain in my Classical Sicilian LTR. See here.} 15. Bg5 b4 16. Ne2 Rb8 17. Nf4 Bb5 18. Rc1 Bxf1 19. Rhxf1 Nd7 20. c4 Nc5 21. Rfd1 Rb6 {I saw the best move here but missed an important detail. Can you do better using the Shankland Method?} *

