21... Rb6 {I saw the best move here but missed an important detail. Can you do better using the Shankland Method?} 22. Qd4 {This was the way, hitting the g7 -pawn. I saw it but disliked the position after ... f6 . I did ask what would happen if I did it anyway, but unfortunately, I answered incorrectly.} (22. Nd3 $2 {let a bit of a chance slip.}) 22... f6 {The computer does not like this move, but it is obviously the critical option.} (22... e5 $2 23. Nd5 {This much is obvious enough.}) 23. Ng6 fxg5 (23... Rh7 {Moving the rook leaves Black statically lost; this is not a challenging move to disarm. The text is the only tough reply.} 24. Be3) 24. Qxg7 {This is the key resource that I needed to see and that I somehow missed. Black loses immediately.} ({I only considered} 24. Nxh8 $2 {, which allows Black to fight back.} Bf6 $1 25. Qf2 gxh4 {I thought Black was totally fine and decided I should look in a different direction. I surely would have won the game if I had used the Shankland Method a bit better.}) *

