26... gxf6 {White's best move certainly does not guarantee a win. I found it and did not win the game. But, it does give the best chance. What would you play?} 27. Qxe6 {Clearly, this is the move White wants to make. It looks like ... Rb6 is a cold shower, but we have to ask, what if I do it anyway?} Rb6 {Does White lose a piece?} (27... fxg5 $2 {I was not so naively optimistic to expect this move to be played, but of course I did have to calculate it.} 28. Qg6+ $1 Kf8 29. Rd5 $1 {Black is crushed.}) 28. Bf4 {Nope! This move lets White remain a pawn up.} *

