1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 a6 8. O-O-O Bd7 9. f3 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 Be7 11. h4 b5 12. Kb1 Qc7 13. Qd2 {The ... h5 idea works against other moves.} (13. g4 h5) (13. Be3 h5) 13... h6 14. Be3 h5 {This strikes me as incorrect. Black loses a tempo, as I explain in my Classical Sicilian LTR. See here.} 15. Bg5 b4 16. Ne2 Rb8 17. Nf4 Bb5 18. Rc1 Bxf1 19. Rhxf1 Nd7 20. c4 Nc5 21. Rfd1 Rb6 {I saw the best move here but missed an important detail. Can you do better using the Shankland Method?} 22. Nd3 {This let a bit of a chance slip.} (22. Qd4 $1 {This was the way, hitting the g7 -pawn. I saw it but disliked the position after ... f6 . I did ask what would happen if I did it anyway, but unfortunately, I answered incorrectly.} e5 $2 23. Nd5 {This much is obvious enough. The computer does not like} f6 {, but it is obviously the critical option. Ng6! fxg5 The only tough reply.} ({(} 23... Rh7 {Moving the rook leaves Black statically lost; this is not a challenging move to disarm.} 24. Be3 {)}) {Qxg7! This is the key resource that I needed to see and that I somehow missed. Black loses immediately. I had only considered Nxh8? , which allows Black to fight back.} 24. Bxf6 $1 {Qf2 gxh4 I thought Black was totally fine and decided I should look in a different direction. I surely would have won the game if I had used the Shankland Method a bit better.}) 22... a5 23. Nxc5 dxc5 24. e5 Rb7 25. Qe2 f6 26. exf6 gxf6 {White's best move certainly does not guarantee a win. I found it and did not win the game. But, it does give the best chance. What would you play?} 27. Qxe6 {Clearly, this is the move White wants to make. It looks like ... Rb6 is a cold shower, but we have to ask, what if I do it anyway?} Rb6 {Does White lose a piece?} (27... fxg5 $2 {I was not so naively optimistic to expect this move to be played, but of course I did have to calculate it.} 28. Qg6+ $1 Kf8 29. Rd5 $1 {Black is crushed.}) 28. Bf4 {Nope! This move lets White remain a pawn up.} Rxe6 29. Bxc7 {The position definitely still should be holdable for Black, and my opponent defended very well to earn his draw. Still, in human terms, White should have some winning chances here, and a headcount should be enough to realize that this was the most promising try.} a4 30. Re1 Kf7 31. Rxe6 Kxe6 32. Re1+ Kf7 33. b3 axb3 34. axb3 f5 35. g3 Bf6 36. Re3 Bd4 37. Rd3 Re8 38. Bf4 Re1+ 39. Kc2 Rg1 40. Rd1 Rg2+ 41. Rd2 Rg1 42. Rd1 *

