31. Nd4 {Black is a pawn down but has a menacing-looking attacking position. What should he play?} Qb3+ {This is clearly the most direct and aggressive attacking move Black has available. It looks like it hangs the queen, but we have to ask: What happens if I do it anyway? Luckily for me, my opponent missed this resource. I had seen it, but I did not think it worked.} (31... Nb3 $2 32. Rd1 $1 {Now White has survived the worst of it and can think about consolidating his extra pawn.}) 32. Nxb3 {Taking on b3 cannot be recommended, but of course, Black should be ready for it.} (32. Ka1 {I had counted on this one, and I thought I was good to go. What did I miss? Question for the next exercise!}) 32... axb3+ 33. Ka1 bxc2 34. Qxc2 Rb3 {White loses a piece, and the game.} *

