44... Bb4 {Despite time control just being reached, I burned a lot of it on calculating the previous critical moment. Here, I miscalculated. Can you use the Shankland Method better than I did?} 45. Rd1 {The answer was that doing it anyway could not be recommended, and this simple move should be preferred.} (45. cxd5 $2 {This is clearly the move I want to make. I saw that a check on a6 would be a problem. I asked what would happen if I did it anyway, and I miscalculated.} Qa6+ $1 46. Qd3 Re8+ $1 {It was at this moment that I realized that my planned Kf1 was not going to work...} 47. Kf3 {A sad necessity. When I took on d5 , I was counting on Kf1? . I thought I had consolidated nicely, somehow missing I am simply mated in 2!} Qxd3+ 48. Rxd3 Re1) 45... Qa4 46. Qd3 dxc4 47. Qf5 Re8+ 48. Kf1 {White has stopped all of the threats.} *

