28. Rxf8 {I correctly used the Shankland Method once already in this game, and now I should use it again. Can you do better than me?} Rxf8 {Obviously, Black would love to take this rook. It looks like Be7 is an issue, but we have to ask, what happens if I do it anyway? I did ask, but I came to the wrong conclusion.} (28... Nf2+ $6 {This was not terrible, and the position is still defensible, but the text was a much cleaner solution.}) 29. Be7+ Kd7 30. Bxf8 Nf2+ 31. Kh2 ({I saw this far and thought I was done for because Nd3 can be met with Re2 . What did I miss?} 31. Kg1 {allows Black to repeat with} Nh3+ {.}) (31. Kg2 $2 {would be a mistake due to} Nd3+ {and} 32. Re2 {is met by} Nf4+ {.}) 31... d4 {White's knight gets kicked, and if it leaves, ... Nd3 becomes the real deal.} 32. Re2 d3 33. Rxc2 dxc2 34. Ne2 Nd3 {Black equalizes.} 35. Bxg7 c1=Q 36. Nxc1 Nxc1 {This endgame should be drawn.} *

