38... Bf7 {I had outplayed my young opponent from a very dry position and reached a promising bishop endgame. White is winning here, but the path is very narrow. Can you find the way?} 39. Bc8 {Shankland Method! Of course, this is the move White wants to make, going after the a6 -pawn. I saw it, and I saw a problem with it. I did ask what would happen if I did it anyway, but I came to the wrong conclusion.} (39. Bd1 Be6 {Now Black has a fortress, no matter how many pawn advances White gets. You can check out the rest of the game next.}) 39... Be6 40. Bb7 {This is the only way. Black is in zugzwang and must lose a critical tempo.} ({Somehow, I had only considered} 40. Bxa6 {, which is obviously natural but not forced.} Bd7 {probably holds too, but Kc6! is very direct and clean. Now, things get very forced. Ke5 Bg4} 41. Bxb5 {Kxb5 Kxd5 Bf3+! and after both Ke5 Kc4 Kf6 Kxd4 Kg7 Kc4 Kxh7 Bh5= and Kd6 Kc4!} Kc7 {Kb5! , Black is making a draw. His control of the long diagonal is too annoying.}) 40... Bd7 {Now what?} (40... Kc7 $2 41. Ke5 {Well spotted.}) (40... Bf7 $2 41. Bxa6 $1 {Now this works since the bishop will get back out.} Kc6 42. Bc8 {.}) 41. Ke3 {We still cannot take on a6 .} (41. Bxa6 Kc6 $1 42. Ke5 Bg4 {transposes to the 40.Bxa6 variation seen above.}) 41... Be6 {Now, Black is ready for ... Kc7 next. But we basically got the move Ke3 for free compared to taking on a6 directly without flicking in Bb7 first. So...} 42. Bxa6 Kc6 43. a4 {Now we see the point of getting the king to e3 . It is in the square of the pawn.} bxa4 44. Kd2 (44. Kd3 $2 Kb6 $1 {All of a sudden, the bishop is trapped! White is lucky not to be lost.}) 44... Kb6 45. Be2 {We can't let Black's bishop reach f5 with a gain of tempo.} (45. Bd3 $2 Bf5 $1 {Black is all too happy to take this diagonal.} 46. Bxf5 gxf5 47. h5 a3 {or Be2 a3} 48. Kc3 a2 49. Kb2 {Bb1= lead to draw.}) 45... Bd7 46. Kc3 Bb5 {And now one final good move seals the deal.} 47. Bg4 {White's king will handle the a -pawn, and the bishop ransacks the kingside. White wins. See the annotated game for details.} ({Note that after} 47. Bd1 $2 a3 $1 {, Black holds because} 48. Kb3 $2 {is not to be recommended:} Ba4+ {Oops.}) *

